WEBVTT

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:05.320
Fletcher has more experience
with propulsion systems.

00:00:05.355 --> 00:00:07.016
But Carstairs is better
with people.

00:00:07.057 --> 00:00:09.025
Considering this is
a supervisory position

00:00:09.059 --> 00:00:10.356
I'd go with her.

00:00:10.394 --> 00:00:11.691
I guess you're right.

00:00:11.728 --> 00:00:14.526
Didn't we just do crew
evaluation reports?

00:00:14.564 --> 00:00:16.532
Three months ago.

00:00:16.566 --> 00:00:18.261
Seems like three weeks.

00:00:20.237 --> 00:00:23.035
Why don't we just
give everybody a promotion

00:00:23.073 --> 00:00:25.098
and call it a night...
Commander?

00:00:25.142 --> 00:00:26.905
Fine with me... Captain.

00:00:26.977 --> 00:00:29.309
Could we have two coffees,
please?

00:00:32.783 --> 00:00:34.216
What could be so funny?

00:00:34.251 --> 00:00:37.482
I mean, what's so funny
about crew evaluations?

00:00:37.521 --> 00:00:39.250
Don't worry about it, Sam.

00:00:39.289 --> 00:00:42.156
Can't we just try
and have a good time here?

00:00:42.192 --> 00:00:44.922
How can I have a good time
when my career is being decided

00:00:44.995 --> 00:00:46.929
across the room?

00:00:46.964 --> 00:00:48.591
Come on. Think promotion.

00:00:48.632 --> 00:00:51.100
Promotion, promotion,
promotion, promotion...

00:00:51.134 --> 00:00:54.035
You can't really believe
that what you're doing

00:00:54.071 --> 00:00:56.938
will influence the outcome
of your evaluation.

00:00:57.007 --> 00:01:00.101
Promotion, promotion...

00:01:00.143 --> 00:01:01.872
It's a time-honored strategy,
Taurik.

00:01:01.912 --> 00:01:04.472
The vedeks of the Janalan
Order maintain

00:01:04.514 --> 00:01:05.674
a round-the-clock chant

00:01:05.716 --> 00:01:07.650
for the benefit
of the Bajoran people.

00:01:09.152 --> 00:01:11.620
Considering the history
of your planet

00:01:11.655 --> 00:01:14.681
that doesn't exactly validate
what he's doing.

00:01:14.725 --> 00:01:17.523
Promote me, please

00:01:17.561 --> 00:01:21.554
so I can make Lieutenant
and have my own room.

00:01:21.598 --> 00:01:24.829
If you are unhappy
sharing quarters with me

00:01:24.868 --> 00:01:28.634
then you should put in
for a new room assignment...

00:01:28.672 --> 00:01:31.038
just in case
you're not promoted.

00:01:35.012 --> 00:01:37.606
I've been thinking
about who to promote to Ops.

00:01:37.647 --> 00:01:39.137
The new night duty officer?

00:01:39.182 --> 00:01:40.911
Mm-hmm.
Lavelle is an obvious candidate

00:01:40.984 --> 00:01:43.077
but I'm also
considering Ensign Sito.

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:44.087
Thank you.

00:01:44.121 --> 00:01:45.088
You're welcome.

00:01:45.122 --> 00:01:46.487
You sure about dessert?

00:01:46.523 --> 00:01:48.650
Yes, don't tempt me.

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:59.259
So, are they working
on crew evaluations?

00:01:59.302 --> 00:02:00.269
Yep.

00:02:00.303 --> 00:02:01.429
Who are they talking about?

00:02:01.471 --> 00:02:02.802
It's not my place to say.

00:02:02.839 --> 00:02:04.136
Come on, Ben.

00:02:04.174 --> 00:02:05.539
Please.

00:02:05.575 --> 00:02:09.033
All right, but I'm not sure
you two are going to like it.

00:02:09.079 --> 00:02:11.570
Apparently, you two are up
for the same job.

00:02:46.249 --> 00:02:50.652
Space, the final frontier.

00:02:50.687 --> 00:02:54.521
These are the voyages
of the Starship Enterprise.

00:02:54.558 --> 00:02:56.526
Its continuing mission...

00:02:56.560 --> 00:03:00.496
to explore strange new worlds

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:04.864
to seek out new life
and new civilizations

00:03:04.935 --> 00:03:09.838
to boldly go
where no one has gone before.

00:04:12.002 --> 00:04:13.526
Lock phasers on target.

00:04:13.570 --> 00:04:14.559
Phasers locked.

00:04:15.572 --> 00:04:16.539
The enemy is firing.

00:04:16.573 --> 00:04:17.540
Helm, hard to starboard.

00:04:17.574 --> 00:04:18.541
Hard to starboard.

00:04:18.575 --> 00:04:19.564
Fire phasers.

00:04:22.379 --> 00:04:24.313
Firing.

00:04:25.682 --> 00:04:27.309
Target is destroyed.

00:04:28.919 --> 00:04:31.513
End simulation sequence.
Secure from drill.

00:04:31.555 --> 00:04:32.988
Alpha shift,
your response time

00:04:33.023 --> 00:04:35.719
was seven percent slower
than the gamma shift.

00:04:35.759 --> 00:04:38.626
All departments,
submit drill evaluation reports

00:04:38.662 --> 00:04:39.890
by 0900 hours.

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:42.091
Ensign, you'll write
that report.

00:04:42.132 --> 00:04:43.224
Yes, sir.

00:04:44.234 --> 00:04:45.724
What happened back there,
Ensign?

00:04:45.769 --> 00:04:46.736
I'm sorry, sir.

00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:47.794
When we changed course

00:04:47.837 --> 00:04:49.896
I had to relock phasers
before I could fire.

00:04:49.973 --> 00:04:52.373
Next time, try letting
the locking relay float

00:04:52.409 --> 00:04:54.502
until the actual order
to fire is given.

00:04:54.544 --> 00:04:57.775
They may not teach that trick
at the Academy, but it works.

00:04:59.082 --> 00:05:00.310
Thank you, sir.

00:05:00.350 --> 00:05:01.544
Lavelle.

00:05:01.585 --> 00:05:02.552
Sir?

00:05:02.586 --> 00:05:04.679
Resume previous course
and speed.

00:05:04.721 --> 00:05:06.018
Aye, aye, sir.

00:05:06.056 --> 00:05:08.456
One "aye" is sufficient,
acknowledgment, Ensign.

00:05:09.893 --> 00:05:12.020
Helm, change course for the
Argaya system, maximum warp.

00:05:12.062 --> 00:05:13.120
Aye, sir.

00:05:13.163 --> 00:05:14.994
What happened to the rendezvous
with the Clement?

00:05:15.031 --> 00:05:16.555
I've received new orders
from Starfleet.

00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:18.227
We'll discuss it
in the observation lounge.

00:05:18.268 --> 00:05:20.566
Mr. Data, Mr. Worf.

00:05:20.604 --> 00:05:22.868
Ensign Sito, take over at Ops.

00:05:22.939 --> 00:05:24.270
Yes, sir.

00:05:33.717 --> 00:05:37.050
The Argaya system's close
to the Cardassian border.

00:05:37.087 --> 00:05:39.078
I wonder why we're going there.

00:05:40.523 --> 00:05:42.616
How would you like
to be a spider

00:05:42.659 --> 00:05:43.887
under that table?

00:05:43.994 --> 00:05:45.894
What?

00:05:45.962 --> 00:05:47.862
A spider under the table.

00:05:47.897 --> 00:05:50.730
Is that like a fly on the wall?

00:05:50.767 --> 00:05:52.962
I guess so.

00:05:56.539 --> 00:05:58.905
You did really well
during the drill.

00:05:59.009 --> 00:06:02.740
Well, apparently
Commander Riker didn't think so.

00:06:02.779 --> 00:06:05.145
I swear he's got it in for me.

00:06:05.181 --> 00:06:06.944
You're imagining things.

00:06:06.983 --> 00:06:09.508
Yeah? Then how come
you're sitting in that chair

00:06:09.552 --> 00:06:10.610
instead of me?

00:06:10.654 --> 00:06:11.848
I guess he figured

00:06:11.888 --> 00:06:14.288
I needed more practice
than you do.

00:06:23.566 --> 00:06:24.863
Excuse me, sir.

00:06:24.901 --> 00:06:26.368
Do you have a minute?

00:06:26.403 --> 00:06:28.030
Sure, Taurik.
What is it?

00:06:28.071 --> 00:06:30.733
I'd like you to take
a look at something.

00:06:33.310 --> 00:06:35.870
Have you been
improvising again, Ensign?

00:06:35.912 --> 00:06:37.379
In a manner of speaking.

00:06:37.414 --> 00:06:39.507
I'm running
a computer simulation

00:06:39.549 --> 00:06:41.881
to test a new warp-field
configuration.

00:06:41.918 --> 00:06:43.545
You got a problem here.

00:06:43.586 --> 00:06:46.885
Your plasma flow to the nacelles
is out of sync.

00:06:46.923 --> 00:06:49.391
Actually, sir,
that was done deliberately.

00:06:49.426 --> 00:06:52.224
As you can see,
this configuration

00:06:52.262 --> 00:06:54.856
has increased
overall warp-field integrity

00:06:54.898 --> 00:06:56.263
by seven percent.

00:06:56.299 --> 00:06:57.357
You're right.

00:06:57.400 --> 00:06:59.368
Dr. Nils Diaz
has been experimenting

00:06:59.402 --> 00:07:00.494
with this technique

00:07:00.537 --> 00:07:02.664
at the Tanaline
Propulsion Laboratory.

00:07:02.706 --> 00:07:04.196
Yeah, I'm familiar
with his work

00:07:04.240 --> 00:07:06.470
but I never heard
anything about this.

00:07:06.509 --> 00:07:09.103
His findings have not
been released yet.

00:07:09.145 --> 00:07:11.841
I was able to review
a preliminary report

00:07:11.881 --> 00:07:13.371
when I was at the Academy.

00:07:13.416 --> 00:07:15.111
I look forward to reading it.

00:07:15.151 --> 00:07:18.314
I predict that when these
findings are made public

00:07:18.355 --> 00:07:21.017
they will become a new model
for warp-field operations.

00:07:21.057 --> 00:07:23.025
Sounds interesting.

00:07:23.059 --> 00:07:24.720
With your permission, sir

00:07:24.761 --> 00:07:27.855
I'd like to begin tests
to see if the technique

00:07:27.964 --> 00:07:30.159
can be adapted
to our warp drive.

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:33.761
There might be variables
that you didn't account for.

00:07:33.803 --> 00:07:36.772
I was quite thorough.

00:07:36.806 --> 00:07:38.797
I'm sure you were,
but I'd still need

00:07:38.842 --> 00:07:41.868
to see your simulation
before I authorize any tests.

00:07:41.945 --> 00:07:44.470
As you wish.

00:07:44.514 --> 00:07:47.881
If you have any other ideas
for increasing efficiency

00:07:47.951 --> 00:07:50.044
don't hesitate
to run them by me.

00:07:50.086 --> 00:07:52.054
As a matter of fact, sir, I do.

00:07:52.088 --> 00:07:54.215
When would be a good time
to discuss them?

00:07:55.592 --> 00:07:57.651
I'll get back to you on that.

00:08:00.029 --> 00:08:01.360
Hmm.

00:08:09.205 --> 00:08:10.832
Excuse me, Doctor.

00:08:10.874 --> 00:08:14.207
If you're wondering
about the evaluations

00:08:14.244 --> 00:08:16.212
things couldn't be better.

00:08:16.246 --> 00:08:18.441
Actually, I just wanted
to tell you

00:08:18.481 --> 00:08:21.848
that Ensign Reilly's condition
is showing improvement

00:08:21.951 --> 00:08:23.248
but thank you.

00:08:23.286 --> 00:08:26.551
In fact, I'm recommending you
for a promotion.

00:08:26.589 --> 00:08:29.114
How does "Lieutenant
Alyssa Ogawa" sound?

00:08:29.159 --> 00:08:31.127
It sounds wonderful.

00:08:31.161 --> 00:08:32.253
I'll talk to Commander Riker

00:08:32.295 --> 00:08:33.523
and I'm sure it'll be official

00:08:33.563 --> 00:08:35.554
as soon as the current
crew evaluations are over.

00:08:37.066 --> 00:08:38.863
Oh, Alyssa...

00:08:38.935 --> 00:08:42.496
how are things going between
you and Lieutenant Powell?

00:08:42.539 --> 00:08:45.997
Fine... I think.

00:08:46.042 --> 00:08:47.566
You think?

00:08:47.610 --> 00:08:52.707
I'm sure it's nothing,
but he seems preoccupied lately.

00:08:52.749 --> 00:08:54.216
Last night,
he had to cancel our date.

00:08:54.250 --> 00:08:56.115
I see.

00:08:56.152 --> 00:08:59.246
He's been putting together
a research proposal.

00:08:59.289 --> 00:09:01.257
He's been really busy with it.

00:09:01.291 --> 00:09:02.815
Well, I know what that's like.

00:09:02.859 --> 00:09:06.659
Sometimes I get so busy
with research, I forget to eat.

00:09:06.696 --> 00:09:08.687
I just wonder...

00:09:12.202 --> 00:09:14.102
What? Sit down.

00:09:18.208 --> 00:09:20.369
I've never met
anyone like Andrew.

00:09:20.410 --> 00:09:23.436
It's as though we've known
each other forever.

00:09:23.480 --> 00:09:26.244
You do seem very well suited.

00:09:26.282 --> 00:09:29.740
But... I know

00:09:29.786 --> 00:09:32.380
that in the beginning
of a romance

00:09:32.422 --> 00:09:34.856
it's possible to be
a little blind.

00:09:34.924 --> 00:09:37.552
I'm not sure
I know what you mean.

00:09:37.594 --> 00:09:41.052
Well... canceling
a date like that...

00:09:41.097 --> 00:09:43.691
the way he's been
so distant lately...

00:09:43.733 --> 00:09:47.464
Doctor, do you think
those could be warning signs

00:09:47.504 --> 00:09:49.631
that he's losing interest?

00:09:49.672 --> 00:09:53.199
Alyssa, I think
you're overreacting.

00:09:53.243 --> 00:09:55.677
Maybe so.

00:09:55.712 --> 00:09:58.510
If I cared about someone
as much as you care about Andrew

00:09:58.548 --> 00:10:00.778
he'd have to do a lot more
than cancel a date

00:10:00.817 --> 00:10:02.148
before I'd get suspicious.

00:10:03.486 --> 00:10:04.544
You're right.

00:10:04.587 --> 00:10:06.885
I'm sure
that when this research is over

00:10:06.956 --> 00:10:09.891
things will be back
just the way they were.

00:10:12.662 --> 00:10:15.426
Except, of course,
that he'll have to deal

00:10:15.465 --> 00:10:16.989
with Lieutenant Ogawa.

00:10:17.033 --> 00:10:18.364
Hmm.

00:10:28.177 --> 00:10:30.270
I only filled in at Ops
for a half hour

00:10:30.313 --> 00:10:32.747
but I had to degauss
the main deflector dish

00:10:32.782 --> 00:10:34.511
recalibrate the navigation grid

00:10:34.551 --> 00:10:37.679
and use internal sensors
to find a lost puppy.

00:10:37.720 --> 00:10:41.019
Ops is a very different
challenge from Tactical.

00:10:41.057 --> 00:10:44.322
I can't figure out
why I'm even being considered

00:10:44.360 --> 00:10:45.759
for this assignment.

00:10:45.795 --> 00:10:48.593
I'm a security officer.

00:10:48.631 --> 00:10:50.622
I recommended you.

00:10:53.303 --> 00:10:55.794
I'll try not to let you down,
sir.

00:10:55.838 --> 00:10:58.170
What could they
be talking about?

00:10:58.207 --> 00:11:01.665
Have you ever considered
learning to lip-read?

00:11:01.711 --> 00:11:03.611
You think Worf's
chewing her out?

00:11:03.646 --> 00:11:05.136
No, he always looks like that.

00:11:05.181 --> 00:11:09.117
Maybe he's giving her pointers
on how to land the Ops position.

00:11:09.152 --> 00:11:10.119
Hi, Will.

00:11:10.153 --> 00:11:11.120
Ben.

00:11:11.154 --> 00:11:12.246
How you doing?

00:11:12.288 --> 00:11:13.448
You call him Will?

00:11:13.489 --> 00:11:14.649
Why not?

00:11:14.691 --> 00:11:16.989
He's second-in-command
of this ship, that's why not.

00:11:17.026 --> 00:11:19.051
I'm not Starfleet;
I'm a civilian.

00:11:19.095 --> 00:11:22.394
When he's in here, he wants
to be treated like a civilian.

00:11:22.432 --> 00:11:24.730
Riker? I bet he sleeps
in his uniform.

00:11:24.767 --> 00:11:27.031
You only think that
because he's your CO.

00:11:27.070 --> 00:11:28.298
If you got to know him...

00:11:28.338 --> 00:11:29.896
Right.

00:11:29.973 --> 00:11:32.441
He's convinced Commander Riker
doesn't like him.

00:11:32.475 --> 00:11:35.069
Why? Did you crash the ship
into something?

00:11:35.111 --> 00:11:36.703
No, he just doesn't like me.

00:11:36.746 --> 00:11:38.179
He doesn't even know you.

00:11:38.214 --> 00:11:40.375
That's right.
You should go talk to him.

00:11:40.416 --> 00:11:41.542
About what?

00:11:41.584 --> 00:11:44.485
Perhaps something
you have in common.

00:11:44.520 --> 00:11:47.717
He likes jazz, poker,
he's Canadian...

00:11:47.757 --> 00:11:49.054
Yeah?

00:11:49.092 --> 00:11:51.117
My grandfather was from Canada.

00:11:51.160 --> 00:11:52.627
There you go.

00:11:52.662 --> 00:11:53.924
Hi.

00:11:53.997 --> 00:11:55.294
Excuse me.

00:11:55.331 --> 00:11:57.629
I got to go talk to somebody.

00:12:03.940 --> 00:12:05.567
Good evening, sir.

00:12:05.608 --> 00:12:07.599
Lavelle.

00:12:10.480 --> 00:12:12.448
Something I can do for you?

00:12:12.482 --> 00:12:15.610
No, sir, I just came
to get another drink.

00:12:15.652 --> 00:12:18.815
Is there something wrong
with that one?

00:12:18.855 --> 00:12:20.152
No. Actually, I...

00:12:20.189 --> 00:12:21.656
What are you having?

00:12:21.691 --> 00:12:22.988
Trakian ale.

00:12:23.026 --> 00:12:25.722
Good choice.
I'll have one, too.

00:12:25.762 --> 00:12:28.890
My grandfather was Canadian,
you know.

00:12:28.931 --> 00:12:30.057
Really?

00:12:30.099 --> 00:12:31.396
Aren't you one, too?

00:12:31.434 --> 00:12:33.402
A grandfather?

00:12:33.436 --> 00:12:36.405
No. Canadian, sir.
Canadian.

00:12:36.439 --> 00:12:39.340
No, I grew up in Alaska.

00:12:39.375 --> 00:12:44.904
Oh. Well... they both...
get a lot of snow.

00:12:44.947 --> 00:12:46.278
Yeah.

00:12:47.784 --> 00:12:50.082
It was good talking to you, sir.

00:12:50.119 --> 00:12:51.450
Yeah.

00:12:52.955 --> 00:12:54.286
Your ale, Ensign...

00:13:02.231 --> 00:13:05.689
We're holding position
in the Argaya system.

00:13:05.735 --> 00:13:07.430
Anything?

00:13:07.470 --> 00:13:10.439
No, sir, I detect no vessels
in the vicinity.

00:13:10.473 --> 00:13:11.872
How close

00:13:11.941 --> 00:13:14.273
to the Cardassian border are we?

00:13:14.310 --> 00:13:16.710
Less than 5,000 kilometers, sir.

00:13:16.746 --> 00:13:21.206
Sir, I'm detecting an object
five meters in length.

00:13:21.250 --> 00:13:23.616
It appears to be an escape pod.

00:13:23.653 --> 00:13:25.848
They must have been forced
to abandon the ship.

00:13:25.888 --> 00:13:28.254
How far inside Cardassian space
is it?

00:13:28.291 --> 00:13:29.781
50,000 kilometers.

00:13:29.826 --> 00:13:32.989
How the hell are we going
to get it out of there?

00:13:40.902 --> 00:13:42.836
Sir, the pod's life-support
system is failing.

00:13:42.871 --> 00:13:43.997
Notify, Dr. Crusher.

00:13:44.039 --> 00:13:45.597
Can we get
within transporter range

00:13:45.640 --> 00:13:47.631
without crossing
into Cardassian territory?

00:13:47.676 --> 00:13:49.075
We would need to boost the gain

00:13:49.111 --> 00:13:51.443
in the confinement beam
by at least seven percent.

00:13:51.480 --> 00:13:53.380
Mr. La Forge?

00:13:53.415 --> 00:13:54.882
I'm on it, Captain.

00:13:54.916 --> 00:13:56.281
There, try that.

00:13:56.318 --> 00:13:58.081
The pod is still too far away.

00:13:58.120 --> 00:14:01.089
Okay, I'm going to try
augmenting the frequency spread.

00:14:01.123 --> 00:14:03.318
Bioreadings indicate
passengers humanoid.

00:14:03.358 --> 00:14:05.349
Attempting life-form
identification.

00:14:05.393 --> 00:14:07.793
No one told you to do that,
Ensign.

00:14:07.829 --> 00:14:10.161
Let's just get them
aboard safely.

00:14:10.198 --> 00:14:12.792
There, that should do it.

00:14:12.834 --> 00:14:15.860
Confinement beam's
at 109% of normal.

00:14:15.904 --> 00:14:17.201
Transporter Room

00:14:17.239 --> 00:14:19.730
you should be able
to get a lock now.

00:14:19.774 --> 00:14:20.832
Aye, sir.

00:14:20.876 --> 00:14:22.844
Dr. Crusher, are you ready?

00:14:22.878 --> 00:14:24.175
Stand by.

00:14:24.212 --> 00:14:27.670
Alyssa, I'm afraid I'm going to
have to ask you to leave now.

00:14:27.716 --> 00:14:29.707
All right, Doctor.

00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:35.053
Transporter Room, go ahead.

00:14:35.090 --> 00:14:36.887
Aye, sir.

00:14:38.126 --> 00:14:40.094
What are you doing here?

00:14:40.128 --> 00:14:41.857
I'm not supposed to let anyone

00:14:41.897 --> 00:14:44.263
but the senior officers
inside Sick Bay.

00:14:44.299 --> 00:14:46.358
Do you have any idea
what's going on?

00:14:46.401 --> 00:14:47.368
No. Do you?

00:14:47.402 --> 00:14:48.528
I better go.

00:14:50.539 --> 00:14:51.836
Ensign.

00:14:51.873 --> 00:14:53.704
Sir.

00:15:02.517 --> 00:15:04.246
1200 hours.

00:15:04.286 --> 00:15:06.550
Alpha shift is relieved.

00:15:09.057 --> 00:15:10.024
Excuse me, sir.

00:15:10.058 --> 00:15:11.025
If you don't mind

00:15:11.059 --> 00:15:12.822
I'd like to stay on
for another shift.

00:15:12.861 --> 00:15:14.351
I could use the training.

00:15:14.396 --> 00:15:15.863
Now's not the best time.

00:15:15.964 --> 00:15:17.829
Yes, sir.

00:15:27.876 --> 00:15:29.935
Ensign, you're with me.

00:15:44.526 --> 00:15:46.460
Bridge.

00:15:51.700 --> 00:15:54.897
You are a certified pilot,
Ensign?

00:15:54.936 --> 00:15:56.927
Yes, sir.

00:16:07.215 --> 00:16:10.013
How long have you served
on board the Enterprise, Ensign?

00:16:10.051 --> 00:16:11.518
Seven months, sir.

00:16:11.553 --> 00:16:12.986
I understand that you've
been recommended

00:16:13.021 --> 00:16:14.113
for the Ops position.

00:16:14.155 --> 00:16:16.020
Do you think you're up to it?

00:16:16.057 --> 00:16:17.354
I do, sir.

00:16:17.392 --> 00:16:18.518
I'm not so sure.

00:16:18.560 --> 00:16:20.187
I'm concerned about your record.

00:16:20.228 --> 00:16:21.752
Sir?

00:16:21.796 --> 00:16:24.731
The incident that you were
involved in at the Academy.

00:16:24.766 --> 00:16:27.291
With all due respect,
that was three years ago.

00:16:27.335 --> 00:16:28.632
My record since then...

00:16:28.670 --> 00:16:31.434
It doesn't matter
how long ago it was, Ensign.

00:16:31.473 --> 00:16:33.304
Would you do something
like that again?

00:16:33.341 --> 00:16:36.504
I can assure you, sir,
that I would never

00:16:36.544 --> 00:16:40.036
never jeopardize lives
by participating in...

00:16:40.081 --> 00:16:41.844
In a daredevil stunt?

00:16:41.883 --> 00:16:43.851
I would certainly hope not.

00:16:43.885 --> 00:16:47.446
But what concerns me is that
you participated in a cover-up

00:16:47.489 --> 00:16:49.889
that impeded
an official investigation

00:16:49.958 --> 00:16:51.653
into the death of a cadet.

00:16:51.693 --> 00:16:53.422
Sir, I know I should
have told the truth

00:16:53.461 --> 00:16:54.485
right from the start...

00:16:54.529 --> 00:16:55.518
Yes, you should

00:16:55.563 --> 00:16:57.121
but you didn't.

00:16:57.165 --> 00:17:00.396
Instead, you joined
with the others

00:17:00.435 --> 00:17:03.632
to pretend that that was
simply an accident.

00:17:03.672 --> 00:17:05.697
Now, what do you
think that tells me

00:17:05.740 --> 00:17:07.207
about your character?

00:17:07.242 --> 00:17:09.540
Sir, if you had any idea

00:17:09.577 --> 00:17:13.138
what it was like
after that incident...

00:17:13.181 --> 00:17:15.581
I didn't have any friends.

00:17:15.617 --> 00:17:18.643
I didn't have anyone to talk to.

00:17:18.687 --> 00:17:21.850
I had to take my flight test
with the instructor

00:17:21.956 --> 00:17:24.584
because no one else
would be my partner.

00:17:24.626 --> 00:17:27.390
In a lot of ways,
it would have been easier

00:17:27.429 --> 00:17:29.454
to just walk away, but I didn't.

00:17:29.497 --> 00:17:30.828
I stuck with it.

00:17:30.865 --> 00:17:33.095
Doesn't that say something
about my character, too?

00:17:33.134 --> 00:17:34.294
Well, I'm really very sorry

00:17:34.336 --> 00:17:37.396
you didn't enjoy your time
at the Academy, Ensign.

00:17:37.439 --> 00:17:38.838
As far as I'm concerned

00:17:38.873 --> 00:17:41.671
you should have been expelled
for what you did.

00:17:41.710 --> 00:17:44.144
Quite frankly, I don't know

00:17:44.179 --> 00:17:48.377
how you made it
on board this ship.

00:17:48.416 --> 00:17:50.213
You're dismissed.

00:18:01.996 --> 00:18:04.726
Another two seconds...

00:18:04.766 --> 00:18:07.701
Okay, that's enough.

00:18:09.537 --> 00:18:12.802
Sir, I'm a little puzzled.

00:18:12.841 --> 00:18:17.039
Why are we intentionally
damaging the shuttlecraft?

00:18:17.078 --> 00:18:20.707
We're evaluating
hull resiliency.

00:18:20.749 --> 00:18:23.274
Starfleet requires
periodic testing.

00:18:23.318 --> 00:18:24.979
I see.

00:18:25.019 --> 00:18:28.648
I don't believe I'm familiar
with that requirement.

00:18:28.690 --> 00:18:33.127
Probably because you're
not a senior officer.

00:18:33.161 --> 00:18:36.062
If you wish,
I can reconfigure the phaser

00:18:36.097 --> 00:18:38.156
to fire a low-intensity burst

00:18:38.199 --> 00:18:40.861
that would not harm
the shuttle's hull.

00:18:40.935 --> 00:18:43.495
The test procedure
would not be affected.

00:18:43.538 --> 00:18:45.802
It's fine just the way it is.

00:18:45.840 --> 00:18:50.436
Now, give me another burst,
about four seconds, right here.

00:18:50.478 --> 00:18:52.469
Do you want me to fire
from this position?

00:18:52.514 --> 00:18:55.540
Actually, why don't you do it
from over here?

00:18:55.583 --> 00:18:58.882
That would be consistent.

00:18:58.987 --> 00:19:01.217
Consistent with what?

00:19:04.392 --> 00:19:05.950
With making it appear

00:19:05.994 --> 00:19:08.792
that this shuttle
had fled an attack.

00:19:12.066 --> 00:19:14.626
What makes you think
that's what we're doing?

00:19:14.669 --> 00:19:16.796
The pattern of fire
you have asked for

00:19:16.838 --> 00:19:18.635
is similar to what might result

00:19:18.673 --> 00:19:20.641
if the shuttle
had fled an attacker

00:19:20.675 --> 00:19:22.734
while engaging
in evasive maneuvers.

00:19:22.777 --> 00:19:26.144
It's an amazing coincidence.

00:19:26.181 --> 00:19:29.207
Yes, sir, it is indeed.

00:19:29.250 --> 00:19:31.548
Shall we proceed
with the testing?

00:19:31.586 --> 00:19:32.848
Yes, Ensign.

00:19:32.921 --> 00:19:34.149
Thank you.

00:19:40.395 --> 00:19:42.386
Alyssa, thank you
for coming so quickly.

00:19:42.430 --> 00:19:43.988
We have to prepare for surgery.

00:19:44.032 --> 00:19:46.694
We have a comatose patient
with a subdural hematoma.

00:19:46.734 --> 00:19:47.860
Yes, sir.

00:19:47.902 --> 00:19:49.733
I want to make it clear
that you are not to discuss

00:19:49.771 --> 00:19:50.863
what you see here with anyone.

00:19:50.905 --> 00:19:51.872
I understand.

00:19:51.906 --> 00:19:52.873
We'll need to synthesize

00:19:52.907 --> 00:19:54.397
at least a liter
of Cardassian blood.

00:20:05.019 --> 00:20:06.577
It's your bet, Taurik.

00:20:06.621 --> 00:20:09.886
What I can't understand is
why we're just sitting here

00:20:09.991 --> 00:20:12.050
so close
to the Cardassian border.

00:20:12.093 --> 00:20:13.720
It must have something to do

00:20:13.761 --> 00:20:15.729
with that escape pod
we picked up.

00:20:15.763 --> 00:20:17.094
Don't you think, Sito?

00:20:17.131 --> 00:20:19.599
Maybe.

00:20:19.634 --> 00:20:21.499
I wonder who was in it.

00:20:21.536 --> 00:20:22.764
You know what I heard?

00:20:23.872 --> 00:20:26.636
It was Ambassador Spock.

00:20:26.674 --> 00:20:27.902
That is most unlikely.

00:20:27.942 --> 00:20:29.432
That's what I was told.

00:20:29.477 --> 00:20:30.444
By whom?

00:20:30.478 --> 00:20:31.445
I can't say.

00:20:31.479 --> 00:20:32.537
They beamed

00:20:32.580 --> 00:20:34.241
whoever was in it
straight to Sick Bay.

00:20:34.282 --> 00:20:36.307
Did you see anything
when you were down there?

00:20:36.351 --> 00:20:38.649
No. Dr. Crusher just asked me

00:20:38.686 --> 00:20:41.177
to help her
with the laboratory schedule.

00:20:41.222 --> 00:20:44.020
I thought Lieutenant Powell
was going to join us tonight.

00:20:44.058 --> 00:20:47.050
He had to do a double shift.

00:20:47.095 --> 00:20:48.255
That's too bad.

00:20:48.296 --> 00:20:50.821
He must be
the worst poker player

00:20:50.865 --> 00:20:51.923
I've ever met.

00:20:52.000 --> 00:20:53.433
It's your bet, Sam.

00:21:03.044 --> 00:21:04.909
Twenty.

00:21:06.247 --> 00:21:07.475
The thing is, I saw Powell

00:21:07.515 --> 00:21:09.073
in Ten-Forward
with another woman

00:21:09.117 --> 00:21:11.483
and the way they were talking,
it made me wonder.

00:21:11.519 --> 00:21:13.009
Well, if he's seeing
someone else

00:21:13.054 --> 00:21:14.021
he should tell Alyssa.

00:21:14.055 --> 00:21:15.386
I mean, it might hurt her now

00:21:15.423 --> 00:21:17.220
but it would be better
in the long run.

00:21:17.258 --> 00:21:18.282
I've been meaning

00:21:18.326 --> 00:21:20.157
to talk to you about something,
Mr. Worf.

00:21:20.194 --> 00:21:22.754
I don't think Ensign Sito's
prepared for the Ops position.

00:21:22.797 --> 00:21:25.891
Well, I must say I disagree,
sir.

00:21:25.934 --> 00:21:29.461
Counselor, pair of fours bets.

00:21:29.504 --> 00:21:30.835
I'm listening.

00:21:30.872 --> 00:21:33.466
The bet is 50.

00:21:40.315 --> 00:21:42.681
It would be illogical
for the Captain

00:21:42.717 --> 00:21:44.207
to deny you a promotion

00:21:44.252 --> 00:21:46.345
for something you did
as a cadet.

00:21:46.387 --> 00:21:49.288
He said it shows
I don't have character.

00:21:49.324 --> 00:21:50.621
What did you say?

00:21:50.658 --> 00:21:54.458
What could I say?

00:21:54.495 --> 00:21:56.190
Maybe he's right.

00:21:56.230 --> 00:21:58.027
Hey, you're a damn fine officer

00:21:58.066 --> 00:22:00.591
and you deserve that post
as much as anyone.

00:22:00.635 --> 00:22:02.967
One thing's for sure.

00:22:03.004 --> 00:22:04.335
I won't be getting it.

00:22:04.372 --> 00:22:05.862
Not if it's up to Riker.

00:22:05.907 --> 00:22:07.374
Well, it is your decision, sir

00:22:07.408 --> 00:22:08.705
but I am certain

00:22:08.743 --> 00:22:10.836
if you give Ensign Sito
a chance to prove herself

00:22:10.878 --> 00:22:12.072
she will not disappoint you.

00:22:12.113 --> 00:22:14.274
Very well, I'll take her
under consideration.

00:22:14.315 --> 00:22:16.875
Besides, I'm not
convinced about Lavelle.

00:22:16.951 --> 00:22:18.213
Really? Why?

00:22:18.252 --> 00:22:19.742
He's too eager to please.

00:22:19.787 --> 00:22:21.880
He's always trying
to ingratiate himself to me.

00:22:21.923 --> 00:22:25.552
Why assume he's doing that
to get the job?

00:22:25.593 --> 00:22:27.754
Fifty.

00:22:27.795 --> 00:22:32.892
Here's your 50, and 100 more.

00:22:33.001 --> 00:22:35.026
I don't know.

00:22:35.069 --> 00:22:37.902
It seems to me that you
and Lavelle are a lot alike.

00:22:37.972 --> 00:22:39.098
What?!

00:22:39.140 --> 00:22:41.267
We're not at all alike.

00:22:41.309 --> 00:22:43.004
You're bluffing.

00:22:44.979 --> 00:22:46.207
You think so?

00:22:46.247 --> 00:22:48.772
Yes, and I'm not going

00:22:48.816 --> 00:22:50.647
to let you get away with it.

00:22:58.259 --> 00:23:00.853
You know, Sam

00:23:00.895 --> 00:23:03.227
maybe you shouldn't try so hard
with Riker.

00:23:03.264 --> 00:23:05.357
It doesn't matter
whether he likes you

00:23:05.400 --> 00:23:06.958
as long as he respects you.

00:23:07.001 --> 00:23:09.765
And he must, otherwise he would
not be considering you

00:23:09.804 --> 00:23:10.998
for the Ops position.

00:23:11.039 --> 00:23:12.404
You're probably right.

00:23:12.440 --> 00:23:15.341
Maybe I'm just telling myself
that he hates me

00:23:15.376 --> 00:23:18.402
so that if I don't get promoted,
I'll have an excuse.

00:23:18.446 --> 00:23:20.243
You in or not?

00:23:20.281 --> 00:23:22.249
At this juncture

00:23:22.283 --> 00:23:27.687
the odds of my winning this hand
are less than 39 to one.

00:23:29.757 --> 00:23:31.782
I fold.

00:23:31.826 --> 00:23:34.317
Commander's flush
is still working.

00:23:34.362 --> 00:23:35.624
No help, Worf.

00:23:36.998 --> 00:23:40.092
Ooh, tens and deuces
for the Doctor

00:23:40.134 --> 00:23:42.261
and jacks and fours
for the Counselor.

00:23:42.303 --> 00:23:44.737
Ah, three sixes.

00:23:44.772 --> 00:23:46.467
Fold.

00:23:46.507 --> 00:23:48.839
Looks like it's just you and me.

00:23:48.876 --> 00:23:50.844
You going to go another 50?

00:23:50.878 --> 00:23:51.845
I'm thinking.

00:23:51.879 --> 00:23:53.141
Give me a second here.

00:23:53.181 --> 00:23:55.308
Didn't you tell me
that you took up poker

00:23:55.349 --> 00:23:57.579
so you could be
in the officer's game

00:23:57.618 --> 00:23:58.607
at the Potemkin?

00:23:58.653 --> 00:24:00.678
I happen to like poker.

00:24:00.722 --> 00:24:03.555
But your senior officers
might have thought

00:24:03.591 --> 00:24:06.856
that you were trying
to ingratiate yourself.

00:24:06.928 --> 00:24:09.055
I guess it's lucky
that they realized

00:24:09.097 --> 00:24:11.224
that you were young
and inexperienced

00:24:11.265 --> 00:24:13.859
and decided not to hold it
against you.

00:24:13.901 --> 00:24:16.199
Hmm.

00:24:16.237 --> 00:24:18.967
Maybe I have been
a little hard on Lavelle.

00:24:20.374 --> 00:24:24.606
I do not believe he is bluffing.

00:24:24.645 --> 00:24:25.737
I do.

00:24:25.780 --> 00:24:27.247
Here you go.

00:24:27.281 --> 00:24:28.771
What have you got?

00:24:30.485 --> 00:24:31.247
Flush.

00:24:31.285 --> 00:24:33.651
I cannot believe this!

00:24:33.688 --> 00:24:35.622
I am your worst nightmare.

00:24:37.125 --> 00:24:38.820
I knew it.

00:24:38.860 --> 00:24:41.488
How could you tell
I was bluffing?

00:24:41.529 --> 00:24:44.396
You don't really expect me
to answer that, do you?

00:24:44.432 --> 00:24:45.421
Look, It's getting late.

00:24:45.466 --> 00:24:46.990
Maybe we should all get
some sleep.

00:24:47.034 --> 00:24:48.899
- One more hand.
- Hmm-mm.

00:24:48.936 --> 00:24:50.460
Come on, Geordi,
you don't have to quit

00:24:50.505 --> 00:24:51.802
just because I'm unbeatable.

00:24:51.839 --> 00:24:54.637
No, there's something I need
to do down in Engineering.

00:24:55.977 --> 00:24:57.604
I'll get you next time.

00:24:57.645 --> 00:24:58.612
I'll be there.

00:24:58.646 --> 00:24:59.908
Good night, everybody.

00:24:59.981 --> 00:25:01.471
Good night.

00:25:03.651 --> 00:25:05.642
Bye.

00:25:05.686 --> 00:25:06.744
Good night.

00:25:06.788 --> 00:25:08.255
See you later.

00:25:12.693 --> 00:25:16.129
What I find curious is that
when Commander La Forge saw

00:25:16.164 --> 00:25:19.827
that the technique I was using
was actually more efficient

00:25:19.867 --> 00:25:21.562
he seemed annoyed.

00:25:21.602 --> 00:25:22.762
Of course he was.

00:25:22.804 --> 00:25:23.771
He didn't like the fact

00:25:23.805 --> 00:25:25.238
that you knew something
he didn't.

00:25:26.607 --> 00:25:27.835
Do you think that I have

00:25:27.875 --> 00:25:30.207
irreparably damaged
my relationship with him?

00:25:30.244 --> 00:25:32.576
Well, it depends
on what kind of a guy he is.

00:25:32.613 --> 00:25:34.547
Ante up, gentlemen.

00:25:35.883 --> 00:25:37.316
Come in.

00:25:37.351 --> 00:25:38.750
Commander...

00:25:38.786 --> 00:25:39.753
As you were.

00:25:39.787 --> 00:25:41.414
I dropped by to see Taurik.

00:25:41.455 --> 00:25:43.252
What can I do for you, sir?

00:25:43.291 --> 00:25:44.656
Well, I'm headed for Engineering

00:25:44.692 --> 00:25:46.216
to run those tests
on the nacelles.

00:25:46.260 --> 00:25:48.660
Since you've already put in
some work on the technique

00:25:48.696 --> 00:25:50.596
I thought you might like
to give me a hand.

00:25:50.631 --> 00:25:53.429
I'd be pleased to, sir.

00:25:53.467 --> 00:25:54.934
Great. Let's go.

00:26:01.309 --> 00:26:04.176
How about some blackjack?

00:26:04.212 --> 00:26:07.306
I've got to get some sleep,
so I can be sharp tomorrow.

00:26:07.348 --> 00:26:10.442
Why? So you can get promoted,
have more responsibility

00:26:10.484 --> 00:26:12.918
and have to get to sleep
even earlier?

00:26:14.422 --> 00:26:15.753
Good night.

00:26:30.238 --> 00:26:32.729
Come in.

00:26:32.773 --> 00:26:34.866
Ben, what are you doing here?

00:26:34.976 --> 00:26:37.308
I just cleaned out
some junior officers

00:26:37.345 --> 00:26:39.609
and I thought
I'd do the same here.

00:26:39.647 --> 00:26:41.877
You're welcome to give it a try.

00:26:41.983 --> 00:26:43.780
Pull up a chair.

00:26:43.818 --> 00:26:45.149
Thanks.

00:26:55.830 --> 00:26:57.764
Dismissed.

00:26:59.266 --> 00:27:00.563
Ensign Sito.

00:27:00.601 --> 00:27:02.159
Yes, sir.

00:27:02.203 --> 00:27:04.034
I also teach an advanced class.

00:27:04.071 --> 00:27:06.631
I believe you may be
ready to participate.

00:27:06.674 --> 00:27:09.142
However, before
you can join the group

00:27:09.176 --> 00:27:10.837
you must pass the gik'tal.

00:27:10.911 --> 00:27:12.208
Gik'tal?

00:27:12.246 --> 00:27:13.372
Yes.

00:27:13.414 --> 00:27:15.575
It is a very ancient
Klingon ritual.

00:27:15.616 --> 00:27:18.813
It tests your knowledge
of the forms of the Mok'bara.

00:27:18.853 --> 00:27:20.582
I should practice first.

00:27:20.621 --> 00:27:21.679
No.

00:27:21.722 --> 00:27:22.950
No practice.

00:27:22.990 --> 00:27:24.855
That is part of the ritual.

00:27:24.925 --> 00:27:27.120
The test must be unannounced.

00:27:33.601 --> 00:27:34.863
Can you see?

00:27:34.902 --> 00:27:35.869
No.

00:27:35.903 --> 00:27:36.892
Good.

00:27:41.642 --> 00:27:43.837
The gik'tal has begun.

00:27:43.878 --> 00:27:45.209
Defend yourself!

00:27:56.557 --> 00:27:59.151
You must anticipate my attack.

00:27:59.193 --> 00:28:00.490
Yes, sir.

00:28:00.528 --> 00:28:02.052
Defend yourself!

00:28:21.315 --> 00:28:23.146
Are you listening, Ensign?

00:28:23.184 --> 00:28:24.481
Yes, but...

00:28:24.518 --> 00:28:26.509
Defend yourself.

00:28:41.735 --> 00:28:43.566
Ow!

00:28:43.604 --> 00:28:45.003
You did not anticipate.

00:28:49.243 --> 00:28:51.074
How am I supposed
to defend myself

00:28:51.111 --> 00:28:52.510
when I can't see a thing?

00:28:52.546 --> 00:28:53.570
Stop making excuses.

00:28:53.614 --> 00:28:54.808
Replace the blindfold.

00:28:54.848 --> 00:28:55.815
No!

00:28:55.849 --> 00:28:58.443
It's not a fair test.

00:28:58.485 --> 00:29:01.079
Very good, Ensign.

00:29:01.121 --> 00:29:04.648
You have passed the challenge.

00:29:04.692 --> 00:29:08.184
What?
By taking off the blindfold?

00:29:08.229 --> 00:29:12.563
It takes courage
to say the test is unfair.

00:29:12.600 --> 00:29:15.831
One thing I don't understand.

00:29:15.903 --> 00:29:19.498
Doesn't gik'tal mean
"to the death"?

00:29:19.540 --> 00:29:21.804
You speak Klingon.

00:29:23.444 --> 00:29:25.139
Sir...

00:29:25.179 --> 00:29:29.411
is there really such a thing
as a gik'tal challenge?

00:29:29.450 --> 00:29:31.543
No, there is not

00:29:31.585 --> 00:29:34.986
but perhaps next time
you are judged unfairly

00:29:35.022 --> 00:29:38.958
it will not take so many
bruises for you to protest.

00:29:47.468 --> 00:29:48.662
All I've ever wanted

00:29:48.702 --> 00:29:51.296
is to make a career for myself
in Starfleet.

00:29:51.338 --> 00:29:54.739
I can't change what happened
at the Academy... no one can.

00:29:54.775 --> 00:29:57.835
All I can do is work hard
and try to earn the respect

00:29:57.878 --> 00:29:59.470
of the people I serve with.

00:29:59.513 --> 00:30:01.447
If you're not going to give me
that chance

00:30:01.482 --> 00:30:02.779
then I respectfully request

00:30:02.816 --> 00:30:04.545
that you transfer me
to another ship.

00:30:04.585 --> 00:30:06.849
If you're looking
for a more lenient commander

00:30:06.887 --> 00:30:08.445
I don't think you'll find one.

00:30:10.858 --> 00:30:13.122
Permission to speak freely, sir?

00:30:16.497 --> 00:30:19.295
Please do.

00:30:19.333 --> 00:30:21.494
If you didn't want me
on your ship

00:30:21.535 --> 00:30:24.868
you should have said so
when I was assigned to it.

00:30:24.905 --> 00:30:28.033
It's not your place
to punish me for what I did

00:30:28.075 --> 00:30:29.269
at the Academy.

00:30:29.310 --> 00:30:31.107
I've worked hard here.

00:30:31.145 --> 00:30:32.874
My record is exemplary.

00:30:32.913 --> 00:30:36.246
If you're going to judge me,
judge me for what I am now.

00:30:36.283 --> 00:30:40.777
Very well, Ensign, I will.

00:30:43.457 --> 00:30:45.687
It took courage
to come here and face me

00:30:45.726 --> 00:30:47.921
after what I said
to you the other day.

00:30:47.995 --> 00:30:51.158
I didn't ask you here
because I was assessing

00:30:51.198 --> 00:30:54.031
your qualifications
for the Ops position.

00:30:54.068 --> 00:30:55.194
I don't understand, sir.

00:30:55.235 --> 00:30:56.896
I was harsh with you

00:30:56.937 --> 00:31:01.271
because I wanted to assess you
for a very important mission...

00:31:01.308 --> 00:31:03.742
a mission that could
put you in a situation

00:31:03.777 --> 00:31:06.871
that would be far more unnerving
than a dressing down

00:31:06.947 --> 00:31:08.437
by your commanding officer.

00:31:08.482 --> 00:31:10.507
Can I ask what that mission is,
sir?

00:31:10.551 --> 00:31:11.882
Join the senior officers

00:31:11.985 --> 00:31:14.317
in the observation
lounge at 0900 hours.

00:31:14.355 --> 00:31:15.720
We'll discuss it then.

00:31:17.257 --> 00:31:18.417
Yes, sir.

00:31:20.060 --> 00:31:21.391
And, Ensign...

00:31:23.097 --> 00:31:27.534
I do know why you ended up
on the Enterprise.

00:31:27.568 --> 00:31:29.092
I asked for you.

00:31:29.136 --> 00:31:31.434
I wanted
to make sure that you got

00:31:31.472 --> 00:31:33.838
a fair chance
to redeem yourself.

00:31:35.876 --> 00:31:37.867
Thank you, sir.

00:31:45.818 --> 00:31:47.183
You wanted to see me, Doctor?

00:31:47.220 --> 00:31:48.380
Yes.

00:31:48.421 --> 00:31:50.321
Alyssa, I think you know

00:31:50.356 --> 00:31:53.917
how much I've come
to depend upon you here.

00:31:53.960 --> 00:31:55.928
I've recommended your promotion

00:31:55.962 --> 00:31:59.261
because your performance
here has been exemplary.

00:31:59.298 --> 00:32:00.595
Thank you, Doctor.

00:32:00.633 --> 00:32:02.032
I appreciate that.

00:32:02.068 --> 00:32:03.467
But more than that

00:32:03.502 --> 00:32:06.596
I've come to think of you
as a friend

00:32:06.639 --> 00:32:09.073
someone I really care about.

00:32:09.108 --> 00:32:13.067
It's nice of you to say that.

00:32:13.112 --> 00:32:15.410
I feel the same way.

00:32:16.782 --> 00:32:18.511
So...

00:32:18.551 --> 00:32:21.520
you and Andrew Powell...?

00:32:21.554 --> 00:32:24.022
Someone told you.

00:32:24.056 --> 00:32:25.614
Told me what?

00:32:25.658 --> 00:32:27.353
We were going
to keep it a secret

00:32:27.393 --> 00:32:29.054
until the promotions
are announced.

00:32:29.095 --> 00:32:30.062
A secret?

00:32:30.096 --> 00:32:31.393
He asked me to marry him.

00:32:31.430 --> 00:32:33.728
Alyssa, that's wonderful.

00:32:33.766 --> 00:32:36.462
I'm so relieved...
I mean happy.

00:32:41.374 --> 00:32:43.001
Please.

00:32:43.042 --> 00:32:44.976
Take a seat, Ensign.

00:32:54.520 --> 00:32:56.852
This is Joret Dal.

00:32:56.889 --> 00:33:00.518
He was in the escape pod
that we retrieved.

00:33:00.559 --> 00:33:03.790
He is a member
of the Cardassian military

00:33:03.829 --> 00:33:05.387
and a Federation operative.

00:33:05.431 --> 00:33:08.423
He has risked his life

00:33:08.467 --> 00:33:10.765
to bring us
invaluable information

00:33:10.803 --> 00:33:13.431
about Cardassian
strategic intentions.

00:33:13.472 --> 00:33:17.033
Information that could very well
enhance the security of Bajor

00:33:17.076 --> 00:33:20.102
as well as other planets
in this sector.

00:33:20.146 --> 00:33:22.114
Now, it is absolutely imperative

00:33:22.148 --> 00:33:25.515
that we return him safely
to Cardassian space.

00:33:25.551 --> 00:33:26.711
It will not be easy.

00:33:26.752 --> 00:33:29.482
The border is heavily guarded.

00:33:29.522 --> 00:33:30.682
Since his ship was destroyed

00:33:30.723 --> 00:33:32.190
he'll be using
one of our shuttles.

00:33:32.224 --> 00:33:35.489
If a patrol stops me,
I will claim to have stolen it.

00:33:35.528 --> 00:33:36.859
We have distressed the shuttle

00:33:36.896 --> 00:33:38.796
so that it appears
to have been fired upon.

00:33:38.831 --> 00:33:42.028
Joret will attempt
to talk his way past the patrol.

00:33:42.068 --> 00:33:46.232
If I were alone, the chances
of my succeeding would be slim

00:33:46.272 --> 00:33:50.368
but if I had a prisoner
with me, a Bajoran terrorist

00:33:50.409 --> 00:33:52.900
I would appear
to be a bounty hunter.

00:33:53.012 --> 00:33:55.742
Border crossings of that nature
are not uncommon.

00:33:55.781 --> 00:33:58.249
And for a price,
the patrol can be convinced

00:33:58.284 --> 00:33:59.683
to look the other way.

00:33:59.719 --> 00:34:01.880
Once the shuttle
is safely past the patrol

00:34:01.921 --> 00:34:04.287
Joret will put you
into an escape pod

00:34:04.323 --> 00:34:06.848
and return you back
across the border.

00:34:06.892 --> 00:34:09.986
Since the pod is so small,
it will be difficult to detect.

00:34:10.029 --> 00:34:11.462
We'll be waiting here
to pick you up.

00:34:11.497 --> 00:34:13.624
I understand, sir.

00:34:13.666 --> 00:34:16.567
Ensign, this is obviously
a very dangerous mission.

00:34:16.602 --> 00:34:19.537
I am not ordering you
to take part in it.

00:34:19.572 --> 00:34:22.871
Then I volunteer, sir.

00:34:22.908 --> 00:34:26.844
Be certain you understand
the risk you are taking.

00:34:26.879 --> 00:34:28.540
If you are captured...

00:34:28.581 --> 00:34:29.878
I'm Bajoran.

00:34:29.915 --> 00:34:33.510
No one knows better than I do
what Cardassians do

00:34:33.552 --> 00:34:36.248
to their prisoners.

00:34:36.288 --> 00:34:39.587
I've made my decision.

00:34:39.625 --> 00:34:41.320
Very well, Ensign.

00:34:41.360 --> 00:34:43.487
Will you report to Sick Bay?

00:34:43.529 --> 00:34:45.190
Dr. Crusher will explain.

00:34:46.232 --> 00:34:48.632
And, Ensign Sito, I must ask you

00:34:48.667 --> 00:34:52.125
not to discuss this mission
with anyone.

00:34:52.171 --> 00:34:54.162
Yes, sir.

00:35:06.252 --> 00:35:09.187
I didn't realize
she would be so young.

00:35:26.505 --> 00:35:28.598
The Captain asked Dr. Crusher

00:35:28.641 --> 00:35:31.633
to make it look
like Joret had mistreated me.

00:35:33.612 --> 00:35:35.307
We're all set here.

00:35:40.553 --> 00:35:42.521
Sir?

00:35:44.356 --> 00:35:47.154
I just want you to know
that I really appreciate

00:35:47.193 --> 00:35:50.060
the fact that you've always
had confidence in me.

00:35:50.096 --> 00:35:52.291
Good luck.

00:35:52.331 --> 00:35:54.265
I'll see you soon.

00:36:31.570 --> 00:36:33.629
We're approaching the border.

00:36:33.672 --> 00:36:36.232
It won't be long
before we're detected

00:36:36.275 --> 00:36:37.936
by the patrol ships.

00:36:40.813 --> 00:36:44.476
When they stop us,
do you want me to say anything?

00:36:44.517 --> 00:36:47.350
No, it should seem
that I've broken your will.

00:36:47.386 --> 00:36:49.354
If you're asked any questions

00:36:49.388 --> 00:36:52.118
Iook at me as though
you're afraid to answer.

00:36:52.158 --> 00:36:54.524
Can I ask you something?

00:36:56.529 --> 00:37:00.989
Why are you doing this...
risking your life for Starfleet?

00:37:01.033 --> 00:37:03.297
I don't consider myself
a traitor

00:37:03.335 --> 00:37:05.667
if that's what you're asking.

00:37:05.704 --> 00:37:08.764
All my life,
I've served in the military.

00:37:08.807 --> 00:37:10.775
Once, it was an institution

00:37:10.809 --> 00:37:13.175
dedicated to the security
of Cardassia.

00:37:13.212 --> 00:37:15.840
Now, it's little more
than a platform

00:37:15.948 --> 00:37:17.506
for ambitious Guls

00:37:17.550 --> 00:37:19.848
hoping to make their reputations
in battle.

00:37:19.919 --> 00:37:21.716
If the information I've provided

00:37:21.754 --> 00:37:24.552
helps Starfleet deter
even one pointless skirmish

00:37:24.590 --> 00:37:25.955
I've served my purpose.

00:37:28.160 --> 00:37:29.991
I'm sick of war.

00:37:31.797 --> 00:37:34.095
My people need peace.

00:37:34.133 --> 00:37:37.193
I never thought I'd hear
a Cardassian

00:37:37.236 --> 00:37:39.329
say something like that.

00:37:41.574 --> 00:37:44.168
And I never thought a Bajoran
would risk her life

00:37:44.210 --> 00:37:45.768
to help a Cardassian get home.

00:37:48.581 --> 00:37:51.607
A patrol ship's moving in
on our position.

00:37:51.650 --> 00:37:53.811
We don't have much time.

00:38:09.802 --> 00:38:11.235
She must have left
on that shuttle.

00:38:11.270 --> 00:38:12.464
There's no other explanation.

00:38:12.504 --> 00:38:13.835
Do you have any idea
where it went?

00:38:13.872 --> 00:38:14.839
Toward Cardassian space.

00:38:14.873 --> 00:38:16.135
That's what I'm worried about.

00:38:16.175 --> 00:38:17.540
Oh, there was one other thing...

00:38:17.576 --> 00:38:20.170
I noticed the shuttle
was damaged...

00:38:20.212 --> 00:38:21.736
Sam, can we talk
about something else?

00:38:21.780 --> 00:38:23.577
Well, don't you care
what's happened to her?

00:38:23.616 --> 00:38:24.674
Of course.

00:38:24.717 --> 00:38:26.344
But we have to accept the fact

00:38:26.385 --> 00:38:27.784
that we're not always told

00:38:27.820 --> 00:38:30.084
about everything that happens
aboard ship.

00:38:30.122 --> 00:38:33.853
Well, we can at least tell
each other what we know.

00:38:38.397 --> 00:38:40.456
Wait a minute.
Do you two know something?

00:38:40.499 --> 00:38:42.364
Sam, please.

00:38:42.401 --> 00:38:44.232
Oh, I can't believe this.
We're friends!

00:38:44.270 --> 00:38:47.501
We're also Starfleet officers.

00:38:47.539 --> 00:38:52.272
I'm not allowed
to talk about it.

00:38:52.311 --> 00:38:53.710
Okay.

00:38:53.746 --> 00:38:55.338
I understand.

00:38:57.516 --> 00:38:59.006
I better get going.

00:38:59.051 --> 00:39:01.611
I got duty in a half an hour.

00:39:04.456 --> 00:39:08.358
Captain's Log, Stardate 47566.7.

00:39:08.394 --> 00:39:12.330
We have reached the coordinates
in Federation space

00:39:12.364 --> 00:39:14.332
where Ensign Sito's escape pod

00:39:14.366 --> 00:39:16.459
was to have
rendezvoused with us.

00:39:16.502 --> 00:39:19.960
However, we have been waiting
for over 30 hours

00:39:20.005 --> 00:39:22.906
and as yet,
there is no sign of her.

00:39:24.877 --> 00:39:26.071
Report.

00:39:26.111 --> 00:39:27.510
We've completed
a long-range scan

00:39:27.546 --> 00:39:28.604
of the area, sir.

00:39:28.647 --> 00:39:32.139
The escape pod doesn't
seem to be out there.

00:39:32.184 --> 00:39:33.674
It is possible
that at this distance

00:39:33.719 --> 00:39:35.209
we are unable
to distinguish the pod

00:39:35.254 --> 00:39:37.484
from the inorganic matter
normally present in space.

00:39:37.523 --> 00:39:39.047
Try narrowing the scan field.

00:39:39.091 --> 00:39:41.355
See if you can pick up
any biosigns.

00:39:41.393 --> 00:39:43.020
Sir, it would help if I knew

00:39:43.062 --> 00:39:45.155
what kind of life signs
to look for.

00:39:45.197 --> 00:39:48.132
You're scanning
for Bajoran life signs.

00:39:48.167 --> 00:39:49.725
Yes, sir.

00:39:53.806 --> 00:39:54.864
Nothing yet.

00:39:54.973 --> 00:39:57.806
The pod is 32 hours overdue.

00:39:57.843 --> 00:40:00.277
Sir, I recommend
we launch a probe

00:40:00.312 --> 00:40:03.179
to increase the range
of our sensor sweeps.

00:40:04.416 --> 00:40:07.044
Launching a probe
into Cardassian space

00:40:07.086 --> 00:40:09.316
would be a treaty violation.

00:40:11.990 --> 00:40:14.185
Mr. Worf, prepare a probe

00:40:14.226 --> 00:40:16.023
and launch when ready.

00:40:16.061 --> 00:40:17.289
Aye, sir.

00:40:21.700 --> 00:40:23.600
Probe launched, sir.

00:40:29.942 --> 00:40:32.274
Sir, I am detecting
signs of debris

00:40:32.311 --> 00:40:35.144
200,000 kilometers
inside Cardassian space.

00:40:35.180 --> 00:40:36.909
Its mass and composition

00:40:36.982 --> 00:40:39.177
indicate it could be the remains

00:40:39.218 --> 00:40:41.812
of a Federation escape pod.

00:40:50.228 --> 00:40:51.855
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:40:51.896 --> 00:40:54.194
We have intercepted
a Cardassian report

00:40:54.232 --> 00:40:57.258
stating that a Bajoran prisoner
escaped her captor

00:40:57.301 --> 00:41:00.930
and was killed
in an evacuation pod

00:41:01.038 --> 00:41:03.973
as she tried to leave
Cardassian space.

00:41:13.851 --> 00:41:17.514
To all Starfleet personnel,
this is the Captain.

00:41:17.555 --> 00:41:20.080
It is my sad duty to inform you

00:41:20.124 --> 00:41:24.185
that a member of the crew,
Ensign Sito Jaxa

00:41:24.228 --> 00:41:26.526
has been lost
in the line of duty.

00:41:26.564 --> 00:41:30.864
She was the finest example
of a Starfleet officer

00:41:30.901 --> 00:41:35.167
and a young woman
of remarkable courage

00:41:35.206 --> 00:41:38.232
and strength of character.

00:41:39.677 --> 00:41:43.909
Her loss will be deeply felt
by all who knew her.

00:41:43.948 --> 00:41:45.609
Picard out.

00:42:14.011 --> 00:42:15.501
You okay?

00:42:15.546 --> 00:42:16.979
Uh-huh.

00:42:25.289 --> 00:42:27.484
I just got promoted.

00:42:27.525 --> 00:42:30.551
Congratulations.

00:42:30.594 --> 00:42:31.583
Thanks.

00:42:32.763 --> 00:42:34.822
It just doesn't feel right.

00:42:34.865 --> 00:42:36.298
For all I know

00:42:36.334 --> 00:42:39.895
she was going to get
the promotion instead of me.

00:42:39.937 --> 00:42:41.529
You shouldn't feel that way,
Sam.

00:42:41.572 --> 00:42:44.063
She would have been
happy for you, Sam.

00:42:44.108 --> 00:42:47.737
The best way to remember her
would be to excel

00:42:47.778 --> 00:42:49.769
in your new position.

00:42:54.585 --> 00:42:56.780
We're proud of you, Sam.

00:43:01.025 --> 00:43:04.893
Excuse me, sir, but I need
to move this table.

00:43:06.630 --> 00:43:08.029
What?

00:43:08.065 --> 00:43:11.330
There's an empty seat
over there.

00:43:15.706 --> 00:43:19.733
I appreciate
what you are trying to do

00:43:19.777 --> 00:43:22.268
but it is not appropriate.

00:43:22.313 --> 00:43:23.871
You were her friends.

00:43:23.981 --> 00:43:26.415
I was only
her commanding officer.

00:43:26.450 --> 00:43:27.815
Sir

00:43:27.852 --> 00:43:31.185
I happen to know that
she considered you a friend.
